WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.710
Revisiting painful memories…

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.330
In the home that she shares with her sister
and niece, Asifa Parveen looks at photos of

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.200
her wedding four years ago.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.480
Her family had to pay a hefty dowry - but
her in-laws and husband didn’t think it

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.480
was enough.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.880
They harassed and abused Asifa.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.160
Finally, her husband Kamran Ali uttered the
word “talaq” or divorce three times over the phone,

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.640
ending their marriage of over
a year in the space of a few seconds.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.980
Asifa Parveen, who was pregnant at the time,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.280
turned to the police but they couldn't do much.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.020
Muslim marriages are usually not registered.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.500
And there is no law banning instant divorce.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.180
“I was shell shocked.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.280
I thought what’s going to happen to me?…My
life is in limbo.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.800
I don’t know where I’m supposed to stay,
what I’m supposed to do, what will happen

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.820
to my daughter?”

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.460
It’s a situation that Niyazmeen is all too
familiar with.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.120
The 29-year-old works in a slum in south Delhi.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.040
She wants to raise awareness about the practice

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.200
of verbal divorce among Muslims and mobilize women.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.680
Today she meets this group.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.280
Most women here are poor, uneducated and were married off young.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.200
Salma Begum is 22.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.780
She suffered years of torture by her in-laws
- ending up in hospital with serious injuries

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.530
and almost completely losing her eyesight.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:36.979
A few months ago, her husband divorced her
- over the phone - and took the younger of

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.020
Salma’s two children with him.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.159
“My husband said I can’t see anymore,
I can’t walk properly.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.620
I even need help to go to the bathroom.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.380
That’s why he divorced me.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.820
He doesn’t want me any more.”

00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:56.319
Niyazmeen says widespread illiteracy and the
stranglehold of patriarchy leaves women highly

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.420
vulnerable when they are abandoned.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.280
“Women have absolutely no rights, they are
left with nothing.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.540
A man just says talaq or divorce three times
and walks away.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.300
Just like that.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.220
He’s free of all responsibility.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.560
He just uses a woman and then dumps her.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.680
He doesn’t pay any maintenance towards his
own children.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.620
This is a huge problem in the Muslim community.”

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.980
The issue has triggered intense debate in
India.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.180
The country’s top court is reviewing the
matter - amid growing calls to ban the practice.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.080
But not everyone agrees.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:44.440
The mid-17th century Fatehpuri Mosque is a
famous landmark in Old Delhi.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:50.230
The imam of the mosque, Mufti Mukarram Ahmad
says triple talaq is an issue of faith and

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.920
personal law - and cannot be tampered with.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.340
“There should be no change in our Muslim
personal law which is Sharia.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.930
This is God’s law.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.900
It’s based on the Koran and on the Prophet’s
sayings…

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:10.100
Women know very well that in the Sharia if there’s a marriage there could well be a divorce.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.480
If you don’t like it, why get married in
the first place?

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.140
There should be no outside interference in
our faith.”

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.980
But that doesn’t fly anymore with women
like Asifa Parveen.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.720
She wants a ban on triple talaq - and a tough
penalty for offenders.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:32.120
So that her daughter is spared a similar ordeal
when she grows up.

